          "criterion_analysis": "EVIDENCE_STATUS: PARTIAL\nRecruiting and Phase 3 are explicitly confirmed by the on-page Search Details text (“Recruiting studies | Phase: 3”) and also consistent with the URL parameter `aggFilters=status:rec,phase:3`. The United States location filter is only evidenced indirectly: the URL includes `country=US` and the first card’s listed sites are in “United States”, but the DOM snapshot does not explicitly show Location = “United States” as an active/selected filter value (e.g., a selected value/chip for Location). Therefore, not all three required filters are “visibly shown as active/selected” based on DOM evidence alone.",
          "discrepancies": "The agent’s narrative claims the Location filter is confirmed as applied (“Location parameter country=US is present in the URL”), but the rubric requires it be visibly shown active/selected; the DOM snapshot does not show an explicit active Location filter selection state, only the URL parameter and U.S. sites in the result card(s).",
          "environment_issues_confirmed": false,
          "condition_verification": true,
          "screenshot_evidence": "DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX: 19\nURL: https://clinicaltrials.gov/search?viewType=Card&aggFilters=status:rec,phase:3&cond=type%202%20diabetes&country=US&sort=updated,desc\nVisible text: “Search Details: Viewing 1-10 out of 30 studies for: type 2 diabetes | Recruiting studies | Phase: 3”\nVisible text within first result card includes locations like “Birmingham, Alabama, United States” and repeated “United States” under Locations.\nVisible control: “Clear Filters (3)”.",
          "screenshot_idx": 19,
          "dom_model_state_idx": 19
        },
        {
          "criterion_analysis": "EVIDENCE_STATUS: PARTIAL\nThe DOM proves two of the three required filters are applied: Recruiting status and United States location. Evidence: URL includes `aggFilters=status:rec` and `country=US`/`locStr=United States`; header text confirms `type 2 diabetes | In United States | Recruiting studies` (DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX 13). However, Phase 3 is not evidenced as applied: the URL does not include `phase:3`, and the Search Details header does not mention Phase 3; the DOM only shows that a Phase 3 filter option exists (`Phase 3 (30)`) without any checked/active state. Therefore, the criterion “Applies all three filters (Recruiting, Phase 3, United States)” is only partially supported by the DOM state provided.",
          "discrepancies": "Agent-predicted output claims Phase 3 and newest-first sorting are applied via `sort=updated,desc` and `aggFilters=status:rec,phase:3`. But DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX 13 shows a different URL lacking both `phase:3` and `sort=updated,desc`, and the Search Details header lacks any Phase 3 mention. Thus, Phase 3 (and sorting) are not supported by this DOM snapshot.",
          "environment_issues_confirmed": false,
          "screenshot_evidence": "DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX: 13 shows URL `https://clinicaltrials.gov/search?viewType=Card&locStr=United%20States&country=US&cond=type%202%20diabetes&aggFilters=status:rec` and page Title `Search ClinicalTrials.gov for: type 2 diabetes, In United States, Recruiting studies | Card Results | ClinicalTrials.gov`, which is explicit evidence that (a) condition query is `type 2 diabetes`, (b) location is `United States` (`country=US`, `locStr=United States`), and (c) Study Status filter is Recruiting (`aggFilters=status:rec`). In the visible results header it explicitly states: `Search Details: Viewing 1-10 out of 304 studies for: type 2 diabetes | In United States | Recruiting studies`. The filter panel lists a `Study Phase` section with an option `Phase 3 (30)`, but in this DOM state there is no explicit indicator (e.g., checked state, active filter chip, or URL `aggFilters=...phase:3`) showing Phase 3 is applied.",
          "screenshot_idx": 13,
          "dom_model_state_idx": 13
        },
        {
          "criterion_analysis": "EVIDENCE_STATUS: PARTIAL\n\nThe DOM explicitly supports that two of the three required filters are applied: Study Status = Recruiting and Study Location = United States (via URL aggFilters=status:rec, URL country=US/locStr=United States, the page title, and the Search Details summary).\n\nHowever, the DOM does not support that Study Phase = Phase 3 is applied in this captured state. The URL lacks an aggFilters entry for phase:3, and the Search Details summary does not mention Phase 3. While “Phase 3 (30)” appears as an available phase option in the filter list, its selected/active state is not evidenced here.\n\nTherefore, only 2/3 filters are proven applied by the DOM, yielding partial support for the criterion.",
          "discrepancies": "The agent’s predicted output claims Phase 3 is applied and that sorting by “Last Update Posted, newest first” is in effect (e.g., referencing sort=updated,desc and “Phase: 3”). In DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX 12, Phase 3 is not present in the URL filters (no phase:3) and “Search Details” does not include Phase 3. This DOM state also provides no evidence about sorting by Last Update Posted (no sort parameter shown and no sort UI state captured).",
          "environment_issues_confirmed": false,
          "screenshot_evidence": "DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX: 12 shows the active query context includes condition term, Recruiting status, and United States location, but does not show Phase 3 applied.\n\nEvidence:\n- URL (state 12): https://clinicaltrials.gov/search?viewType=Card&locStr=United%20States&country=US&cond=type%202%20diabetes&aggFilters=status:rec\n  - Contains cond=type%202%20diabetes\n  - Contains country=US and locStr=United%20States\n  - Contains aggFilters=status:rec\n  - Does NOT contain phase:3 in aggFilters.\n- Page Title (state 12): “Search ClinicalTrials.gov for: type 2 diabetes, In United States, Recruiting studies | Card Results | ClinicalTrials.gov” (explicitly confirms Recruiting + United States + type 2 diabetes).\n- “Search Details” line (state 12): “Search Details: Viewing 1-10 out of 304 studies for: type 2 diabetes | In United States | Recruiting studies” (again confirms Recruiting + United States + type 2 diabetes, but no Phase 3).\n- Filter UI text present (state 12): under Study Phase, the option “Phase 3 (30)” is listed, but the DOM snapshot does not provide an explicit checked/selected state for that option in this state.",
          "screenshot_idx": 12,
          "dom_model_state_idx": 12
        },
        {
          "criterion_analysis": "EVIDENCE_STATUS: PARTIAL\nThe DOM supports that two of the three required filters are applied: (1) Study Status = Recruiting is supported by the URL parameter `aggFilters=status:rec` (DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX: 10, URL), and (2) Study Location = United States is supported by `country=US` and `locStr=United%20States` in the URL (DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX: 10, URL/title: “In United States, Recruiting studies”). However, the DOM snapshot does not support that Study Phase = Phase 3 is applied: Phase 3 appears only as an available facet (`Phase 3 (30)` in the filter list), and the URL lacks any phase filter (no `aggFilters=...phase:3`). Therefore, the criterion “applies all three filters (Recruiting, Phase 3, United States)” is only partially evidenced in the DOM for this state.",
          "discrepancies": "Criterion requires Phase 3 to be applied and visibly active. In DOM_MODEL_STATE_INDEX: 10, Phase 3 is not evidenced as active/applied (no `phase:3` in `aggFilters`, and no explicit selected-state text for the Phase 3 checkbox), even though the option `Phase 3 (30)` is present as an available filter. Recruiting and United States are evidenced as applied via URL parameters.",
