    "step8_outcome_verification": {
      "primary_intent": "Return the top three ClinicalTrials.gov search results for “type 2 diabetes” after applying the exact filters (Recruiting, Phase 3, United States) and sorting by “Last Update Posted” newest-first, and report for each result its NCT number, full title, study status, and the Last Update Posted date as displayed. A reasonable user would not be flexible on missing the Last Update Posted dates, wrong ordering, or reporting results not actually shown under the specified filtered/sorted view.",
      "reasoning": "Nitpicks: The agent relying on URL parameters (e.g., sort=updated,desc; country=US) rather than a visibly labeled sort dropdown/chip is a minor issue if the resulting list and required fields are correctly captured. Also, the filter UI not explicitly showing a “United States” chip while the URL includes country=US is a minor UI-evidence gap if the final results clearly correspond to US-only.\n\nCritical issues: (1) Missing required fields: the agent did not provide the “Last Update Posted” date for any of the three studies, explicitly stating it was “not explicitly shown.” This is a hard requirement and the primary deliverable includes those dates. (2) Unverified / likely fabricated titles for results #2 and #3: In the final filtered/sorted state (DOM state 20), NCT07664553 and NCT06739122 appear, but their full titles are not visible in the provided DOM evidence; the agent nevertheless outputs full titles for both, which are not supported by the DOM excerpts and therefore count as unsupported claims. (3) Stopping condition not met: the task required stopping only after recording all requested fields; since Last Update Posted dates were not recorded, the agent stopped prematurely relative to the task’s explicit stopping condition.\n\nWhat was accomplished: The agent did reach a ClinicalTrials.gov results page for “type 2 diabetes,” and later reached a URL that clearly encodes the intended filters and sort (DOM states 19–20 show aggFilters=status:rec,phase:3 and sort=updated,desc, plus country=US). The top result’s NCT (NCT07662213), title, and Recruiting status are supported by DOM state 20. The NCT IDs and Recruiting status for #2 (NCT07664553) and #3 (NCT06739122) are also supported by DOM state 20. However, because the required Last Update Posted dates were not captured at all, and because two of the three “full titles” are not evidenced, an average user would not consider the task completed— they asked specifically for the Last Update Posted dates and accurate reporting of the first three displayed results with those fields.",
